.\" -*- coding: UTF-8 -*-
.TH SWPASSKEYCTL 1 "2026-11-04" "swpasskey 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
swpasskeyctl \- inspect and control the local swpasskey authenticator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B swpasskeyctl
.RB [ \-\-socket " " PATH ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.I command
.RI [ argument ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Communicate with the user's running swpasskeyd through its Unix control socket.
Run as the same ordinary user as the daemon. No administrator privileges are
needed. This command does not start the daemon.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show command help.
.TP
.BI \-\-socket " path"
Select the control socket, overriding SWPASSKEY_CTL_SOCKET.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the raw JSON response for any command. For list, this includes full IDs.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
List stored credentials, including site, user, credential ID and key backend.
The displayed ID is a unique prefix at the time of listing.
.TP
.B stats
Show counters, selected key backend and credential counts. For the Debian
service, verify that the backend is TPM.
.TP
.B set-pin
Set or replace the CTAP PIN, prompting twice with terminal echo disabled.
Requires presence approval through the daemon. The local control operation does
not ask for the old PIN. Never supply the PIN as a command-line argument or
paste it into logs or chat. Setting a PIN does not replace existing credentials.
.TP
.BI delete " credential-id"
Delete one credential by a unique hexadecimal prefix of 4 to 64 characters.
Case is ignored. If multiple IDs match, provide more characters. Deletion is
irreversible locally and does not remove the corresponding website registration.
There is no separate presence confirmation for this command.
.TP
.B reset
Reset the authenticator after presence approval. Clears credentials and PIN
state; existing website registrations will no longer authenticate. Use only
when intentionally discarding this authenticator.
.TP
.BI log-level " level"
Change the running daemon's log level: error, warn, info, or debug. The change
is not persisted across daemon restarts.
.TP
.B quit
Ask the daemon to exit. Does not disable future login startup.
.SH EXAMPLES
Inspect the authenticator and set a PIN interactively:
.PP
.nf
swpasskeyctl stats
swpasskeyctl list
swpasskeyctl list --json
swpasskeyctl set-pin
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SWPASSKEY_CTL_SOCKET
Override the default control socket.
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Default socket is $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/swpasskey/ctl.sock. Without this variable,
uses the data directory ($XDG_DATA_HOME/swpasskey, or ~/.local/share/swpasskey).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on a communication or daemon-reported failure, and 2 for detected
command-line usage errors, including mismatched PIN confirmation.
.SH SECURITY
The PIN and presence prompt are software checks, not TPM-enforced authorization.
Keep an independent recovery method. Stop the service before removing the
package; removing it does not erase user data or revoke website credentials.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR swpasskeyd (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1)
